hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"531","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Habib, from one of our shaykhs, who said: Whenever a pleasing matter came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: Praise be to Allah, the Bestower, the Generous, by whose blessings good deeds are completed; and when a displeasing matter came to him, he would say: Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. Abu Dawud said: It has been narrated with a connected chain, and in it are weak hadiths, and it is not sound."
